                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]TL;DR Don't buy this game, buy Siberian Mayhem instead[/h1]\n\nOther than fighting with the graphics settings because this is somehow one of the least optimized games I own, it's no jankier than Serious Sam 3 in terms of stability. However, the overall game design is somehow a million times worse. Playing this game honestly made me think that the developers somehow mysteriously forgot everything about their previous games and why they were good. I have no idea how this game has 84% positive reviews at the time of me posting this.\n\nWithin the first 30 minutes, I probably skipped at least 25 cutscenes; for a Serious Sam game, that's absurd. The dialogue from all of the unnecessary companion NPCs is incessant and never-ending. The pacing is mind-numbing and grueling. The map design and enemy placement are baffling. The maps will either be enormous for no reason or extremely cramped for no reason, and both simultaneously somehow feel completely unsuitable for the fights the game throws at you.\n\nHaving played Siberian Mayhem first and then Serious Sam 4 second, it's no wonder they brought in a different team to make something else. Siberian Mayhem was made by a team of Serious Sam community modders and it's blatantly obvious they understood the idea of a good Serious Sam game more than Croteam did. I really wanted to give this game a chance because I love Serious Sam games, but this is just incredibly lousy.\n\nYou have absolutely no reason to buy this over Siberian Mayhem, do yourself a favor and pretend this game doesn't exist. It is slow, annoying, and will try your patience for all the wrong reasons.\n\nJust buy this instead: https://store.steampowered.com/app/1792250/Serious_Sam_Siberian_Mayhem/",
